{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20060",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.62,
      "end_seconds": 7.25,
      "duration_seconds": 6.63,
      "text": "doctor, this one's ready for you everything's on the chart, but I'll go through it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.98,
      "end_seconds": 12.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "okay, thanks. Hi, how can I help today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.75,
      "end_seconds": 21.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.87,
      "text": "Well, I've been having a sore on the bottom of my foot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.99,
      "end_seconds": 35.11,
      "duration_seconds": 12.12,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse. It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.8,
      "end_seconds": 46.62,
      "duration_seconds": 6.82,
      "text": "I notice it more with walking. Keeping off it helps a bit"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.01,
      "end_seconds": 50.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "is it accompanied by anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.74,
      "end_seconds": 77.59,
      "duration_seconds": 25.85,
      "text": "It usually comes with numbness in my feet. The numbness in my feet? That's been for one week. And I've been feeling feverish as well uh for about two weeks. Um uh about feeling feverish maybe a three out of ten on a bad day. Only paracetamol and it's not much."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 86.94,
      "end_seconds": 97.36,
      "duration_seconds": 10.42,
      "text": "Doctor I've got the readings for you. Weight 52 kilos BP is 109 over 77 temperature 38.3 height 182 centimetres pulse is 88 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.66,
      "end_seconds": 99.36,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.06,
      "end_seconds": 104.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second make yourself comfortable"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.4,
      "end_seconds": 106.33,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "sure thing"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.3,
      "end_seconds": 109.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.81,
      "end_seconds": 125.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.43,
      "text": "The pulses at the ankle are weak but I can feel them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.87,
      "end_seconds": 129.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "stay as you are for a moment"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.62,
      "end_seconds": 155.72,
      "duration_seconds": 7.1,
      "text": "there is a two-centimetre ulcer on the ball of the right foot with redness around it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.16,
      "end_seconds": 165.2,
      "duration_seconds": 6.04,
      "text": "you can sit up now. A few quick ones: confusion, calf pain or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.0,
      "end_seconds": 174.16,
      "duration_seconds": 7.16,
      "text": "okay, so no confusion, calf pain or chest pain, none of it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.48,
      "end_seconds": 181.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.79,
      "text": "right, have you had any vomiting or pain at rest in the leg?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.79,
      "end_seconds": 190.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "I haven't had vomiting or pain at rest in the leg no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.01,
      "end_seconds": 193.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "how are your bowels any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.42,
      "end_seconds": 197.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "No, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.46,
      "end_seconds": 202.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.58,
      "end_seconds": 208.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "ah, my cousin has psoriasis. My grandmother had dementia"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.77,
      "end_seconds": 213.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "what line of work are you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.37,
      "end_seconds": 220.6,
      "duration_seconds": 5.23,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.52,
      "end_seconds": 227.55,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "Alright, what does a a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.46,
      "end_seconds": 232.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.15,
      "end_seconds": 235.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.93,
      "end_seconds": 239.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.66,
      "end_seconds": 256.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "right, before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 257.76,
      "end_seconds": 263.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.42,
      "text": "sorry, what was I saying, no, I've never reacted to anything"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.94,
      "end_seconds": 268.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 269.0,
      "end_seconds": 277.13,
      "duration_seconds": 8.13,
      "text": "Yes, diabetes. High blood pressure, for nearly five years. High cholesterol, for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.23,
      "end_seconds": 289.96,
      "duration_seconds": 11.73,
      "text": "right, so high blood pressure and high cholesterol are already on your record we'll keep that in mind today tell me your medicines, please"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.66,
      "end_seconds": 296.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "Metformin, 500 milligrams, twice a day for my sugar"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 296.83,
      "end_seconds": 302.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.44,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 1000 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.65,
      "end_seconds": 307.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "I see. Is the most recent prescription on you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 308.78,
      "end_seconds": 321.3,
      "duration_seconds": 12.52,
      "text": "No I left it it at home. Mm I take telmisartan 40 milligrams once a day for my pressure. I'm on rosuvastatin 10 milligrams maybe at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.15,
      "end_seconds": 326.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Is the packet here, or the prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 327.49,
      "end_seconds": 331.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "not with me. I'll bring it next time"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.85,
      "end_seconds": 377.86,
      "duration_seconds": 29.01,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. It fits best with an infected diabetic foot ulcer. Pressure damage is also on my list. I'll request blood tests, it'll help with infection. We should do a swab from the ulcer for infected ulcer. We'll begin with amoxicillin/clavulanic acid, 625 milligrams, three times a day, for seven days. That should help with foot infection. Keep the weight off that foot and keep the dressing dry."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 378.94,
      "end_seconds": 387.5,
      "duration_seconds": 8.56,
      "text": "and please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit so we can settle the dose"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 389.07,
      "end_seconds": 390.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 393.88,
      "end_seconds": 402.35,
      "duration_seconds": 8.47,
      "text": "Come back or go to emergency straight away if the redness spreads or you feel unwell with a fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 404.3,
      "end_seconds": 406.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "thank you, that's clear"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 407.0,
      "end_seconds": 409.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 411.45,
      "end_seconds": 414.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "great, thank you for your help"
    }
  ]
}